Subject: [08/14] reports: re-rank all runs with the plane estimator (no new
 MD)

Applying tools/tbr_plane.py to the second half of every existing production
segment re-orders the scan and flags the broken early protocols (negative
TBR_eff = inverted gradient).  Within protocol v1.6, P350 is 6.2 % above flat.
---
 reports/rerank_plane_estimator_2026-11-12.txt | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 reports/rerank_plane_estimator_2026-11-12.txt

diff --git a/reports/rerank_plane_estimator_2026-11-12.txt b/reports/rerank_plane_estimator_2026-11-12.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0fcbc92
--- /dev/null
+++ b/reports/rerank_plane_estimator_2026-11-12.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Re-rank of every run in anchor/workspace with the interface-model-free
+estimator tools/tbr_plane.py (TBR_eff = [T(-84A) - T(+84A)] / q), computed on
+the second half of each production segment.  No new MD was run.
+
+Notes:
+  * negative values (run_v001/v009/v010) are the early broken protocols whose
+    temperature gradient was inverted -- the estimator detects that correctly;
+  * protocol generations do not agree with each other (v1.3 5-8e-9,
+    v1.4/v1.5 1.3-1.4e-8, v1.6 1.5-1.6e-8) because the interface keeps coarsening
+    with time; only within one protocol are the numbers comparable;
+  * in v1.6 (the only properly equilibrated protocol) P350 is 6.2 % ABOVE flat.
